TODO — no licence has been chosen yet.

The requirement, stated so it survives until counsel is involved: copyleft with
no enclosure. The corpus curation, the schema, and the engines are meant to
stay open — improvements return to the commons, and no party (including the
authors) gets to close what others contributed to. Candidate licences must be
evaluated against that requirement by someone qualified to do so; this file is
deliberately a placeholder rather than a guess, because a licence is a legal
instrument and committing one without review is worse than committing none.

Until a licence is committed, default copyright applies: all rights reserved.
